  "assessments": [
    {
      "scope": "Review authority and mission",
      "assessment": "Accepted within the explicit user-authorized completion task. Review uses the existing trusted-base contributor/product/security/evaluation contracts. Proposed PR-head review policy is code under review, never authority to approve itself. This record is an agent assessment performed through the authenticated owner account, not an independent human review or an invented model, audit, Santa verdict or subagent result."
    },
    {
      "scope": "CODEOWNERS and Copilot instructions",
      "assessment": "CODEOWNERS routes all paths to the existing ecorp-team and explicitly does not claim to enforce approval itself. Copilot instructions identify the PR-head trust boundary, require a trusted-base or independent owner assessment for policy changes, and do not confer remote mutation permissions. Native branch requirements remain external to the PR."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Root, web and Rust contributor instructions",
      "assessment": "Root invariants remain intact. The command replacement pnpm check resolves through tools/run_checks.mjs and the validation configuration to the original migrations, format, workspace Clippy/tests, web build and lint gates, plus audit compatibility, local EVM and documentation checks. Web instructions retain explicit actor/Corp/mission/source scope and producer/verifier separation. Rust instructions retain crate boundaries, actual test-count disclosure and owned native fixtures."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Code-review package and upstream resources",
      "assessment": "Packaged resources supply advisory review/remediation rubrics with explicit evidence and capability requirements. Missing capabilities do not become fictional audit completion. The remediation guidance does not supersede this task's existing authorization or the explicit no-subagent constraint. The package cannot approve its own changes or issue an independently authenticated owner decision."
    },
    {
      "scope": "executor-snapshot.mjs",
      "assessment": "The helper performs read-only GitHub API inventory using the native gh transport, validates required identities and pagination, and suppresses raw diagnostic output. Snapshot data is not merge authority. No remote write, alternative scheduler or secret-bearing token argument was found in the reviewed implementation."
    },
    {
      "scope": "executor-state.mjs and git-ref.mjs",
      "assessment": "These are local journal/receipt and ref-format helpers. Review covered native locking, append-history retention, source/review fences, atomic state writes, stable operation identities, interrupted-operation recovery and refusal of self-issued authenticity claims. They do not implement a remote scheduler or mint reviewer authorization. The configured test discovery includes their security and recovery regressions."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Readiness guidance",
      "assessment": "The readiness skill is measurement-only: it reports source, evidence, coverage and limitations. It does not confer permissions or turn line counts, configured checks or historical evidence into executed acceptance."
    },
    {
      "scope": "CI, repository checks and evidence workflow",
      "assessment": "The original quality, integration, Ubuntu/Windows/macOS runner and desktop-Windows jobs remain. Native fixture checks and evidence-scanner lanes are added. Node discovery includes tooling, web, steward, readiness and .github/skills tests. Only the dedicated Keycloak live fixture and immutable historical PR226 replay are excluded with explicit separate-lane disclosure. The Linux SQLx lane keeps worker/gateway acceptance and supplies checksum/version-pinned Anvil; no missing fixture is hidden by skipping that test."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Security workflow and snapshot exceptions",
      "assessment": "Security uses checksum-pinned Gitleaks and the repository's native default CodeQL setup; it does not introduce a conflicting advanced upload job. Current source snapshots and detector canaries remain required. Historical/synthetic snapshot exceptions are individually constrained by anchored path AND full-match value patterns. Historical artifacts remain unchanged, and full CodeQL alert dispositions are separately recorded with their actual reasons."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Merge decision limits",
      "assessment": "No policy-source regression requiring a further edit remains in this reviewed delta. This accepts the policy portion only. Final acceptance still requires current-source validation, hosted CI/security completion and exact-head checks. The user authorized reviewer-only overrides; this assessment does not authorize weakening required CI/security checks or rewriting contributor ancestry."
    }
  ],
  "final_head_binding": "Before publishing this review, verify the final head preserves every reviewed policy and supporting-source blob and that its trusted-base policy diff has this same digest. Evidence-only additions do not become product execution evidence."
}
